# AI_elicit_log

What the AI included that wasn't thought of before
1 - Part of Speech of words
2 - Example Sentence for words
3 - Alternate Forms of words
4 - User data should be kept when exiting the app
5 - The interface working on mobile and desktop screens
6 - Users can see all vocabulary in a table

Questions the AI asked that wasn't thought of before
1 - Is the app for one user or multiple accounts?
2 - Should it include a preloaded JLPT N5 vocabulary list?
3 - Does “known” mean completed, or can users mark a word known without studying it?
4 - Should progress be based only on “known” words?
5 - Are spaced-repetition quizzes or flashcards required?
6 - Should vocabulary be importable/exportable?
7 - Which interface languages must be supported initially?

Answers for the AI Questions
1 - For one user
2 - Yes
3 - Known means completed
4 - Yes
5 - Flashcards required
6 - Should be made where you can create and delete words known
7 - English, Spanish, Japanese, Chinese

What the AI included that will not be a part of this project
1 - Alternate Forms of words because there are too many to learn accurately
2 - Grammar conjugations
3 - Example sentences of words

What the AI included that will be a part of this project
1 - Part of speech of wards
2 - User data should be kept when exiting the app
3 - The user interface works for both mobile and desktop screens
4 - Users can see all vocabulary inside a table
